{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lrwiv6eLsWKjpivVooQKAw","type":"tool_result","content":"455\t  is no plan in this release with a structural cure. The maintainer settings\n456\t  template still ships 90; the framework repository's own settings now use\n457\t  3650, and installs do not receive that file. The protection is still a\n458\t  scheduled backup with `ceo-backup.sh`.\n459\t\n460\t### What an adopter should know before installing or upgrading\n461\t\n462\t- Coming from v1.4.2, read `[1.4.3]` too. Its notes apply.\n463\t- The requirements are unchanged: Claude Code 2.1.280 or later, Python 3.9\n464\t  or later, and Node.js 20 or later for the npm shim.\n465\t- A command that reaches `rm -rf`, `git reset --hard` or a forced\n466\t  `git push` indirectly may now be blocked, and so may a shell body the\n467\t  guard cannot parse. To turn the scan off, set\n468\t  `CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_GUARD=0`, or only the heuristics with\n469\t  `CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_HEURISTICS=0`, in the environment Claude Code starts\n470\t  with. Each disable is recorded once per session.\n471\t- If you patched a hook by hand, re-apply the patch to its module. The\n472\t  modules behind the seven kernel entry points, the five flat modules\n473\t  above and `_lib/adapters/live/` are kernel paths now: a sentinel alone\n474\t  no longer unlocks them; they need `CEO_KERNEL_OVERRIDE` with\n475\t  `CEO_KERNEL_OVERRIDE_ACK=I-ACCEPT`.\n476\t- If your code reads `Finding.start` and `Finding.end` from\n477\t  `secret_patterns.scan()`, they now index the text you passed in, not its\n478\t  NFKC form.\n479\t- Expect a yellow `main_checkout_state` in `/ceo-boot` when your main\n480\t  checkout is on a feature branch.\n481\t- `ceo-restore.sh` previews by default; pass `--apply` to restore. Keep your\n482\t  own copy of `audit-key` and `.salt`, because the backup leaves them out.\n483\t- The VETO floor now admits retired model ids. If your veto roles must not\n484\t  run on them, check the `model:` of your agent files yourself.\n485\t- The model allowlist now admits other vendors' ids (Gemini, Grok) and\n486\t  retired Claude 4 ids. `/ceo-boot` no longer reports a model variable set\n487\t  to one of them as `settings_tamper_model_remap`, and `validate-governance.sh`\n488\t  accepts such a `model:` in an agent file. If you rely on that tamper\n489\t  finding, check the model variables of your settings yourself.\n490\t- If you rely on the audit trail for longer than 30 days, raise\n491\t  `cleanupPeriodDays` at user scope and back up the audit files.\n492\t\n493\t## [1.4.3] - 2026-10-15\n494\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50141584-ed08-437c-bb91-f56d610ea253","uuid":"b0fa5257-267a-4b95-8d2c-d93dc9ac1e86","timestamp":"2026-11-13T18:39:56.650Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/CHANGELOG.md","content":"  is no plan in this release with a structural cure. The maintainer settings\n  template still ships 90; the framework repository's own settings now use\n  3650, and installs do not receive that file. The protection is still a\n  scheduled backup with `ceo-backup.sh`.\n\n### What an adopter should know before installing or upgrading\n\n- Coming from v1.4.2, read `[1.4.3]` too. Its notes apply.\n- The requirements are unchanged: Claude Code 2.1.280 or later, Python 3.9\n  or later, and Node.js 20 or later for the npm shim.\n- A command that reaches `rm -rf`, `git reset --hard` or a forced\n  `git push` indirectly may now be blocked, and so may a shell body the\n  guard cannot parse. To turn the scan off, set\n  `CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_GUARD=0`, or only the heuristics with\n  `CEO_BASH_INDIRECT_HEURISTICS=0`, in the environment Claude Code starts\n  with. Each disable is recorded once per session.\n- If you patched a hook by hand, re-apply the patch to its module. The\n  modules behind the seven kernel entry points, the five flat modules\n  above and `_lib/adapters/live/` are kernel paths now: a sentinel alone\n  no longer unlocks them; they need `CEO_KERNEL_OVERRIDE` with\n  `CEO_KERNEL_OVERRIDE_ACK=I-ACCEPT`.\n- If your code reads `Finding.start` and `Finding.end` from\n  `secret_patterns.scan()`, they now index the text you passed in, not its\n  NFKC form.\n- Expect a yellow `main_checkout_state` in `/ceo-boot` when your main\n  checkout is on a feature branch.\n- `ceo-restore.sh` previews by default; pass `--apply` to restore. Keep your\n  own copy of `audit-key` and `.salt`, because the backup leaves them out.\n- The VETO floor now admits retired model ids. If your veto roles must not\n  run on them, check the `model:` of your agent files yourself.\n- The model allowlist now admits other vendors' ids (Gemini, Grok) and\n  retired Claude 4 ids. `/ceo-boot` no longer reports a model variable set\n  to one of them as `settings_tamper_model_remap`, and `validate-governance.sh`\n  accepts such a `model:` in an agent file. If you rely on that tamper\n  finding, check the model variables of your settings yourself.\n- If you rely on the audit trail for longer than 30 days, raise\n  `cleanupPeriodDays` at user scope and back up the audit files.\n\n## [1.4.3] - 2026-10-15\n","numLines":40,"startLine":455,"totalLines":2658}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Lrwiv6eLsWKjpivVooQKAw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
