function on 3.9+, is correctly skipped by the __module__ test.\\n- No circular import, standard library only, and the syntax works on Python 3.9.\\n- Fail direction is not inverted:\\n  - every Rule 1 error is wrapped as RuleOneInputError, re-raised `from None` as PersonalPathUnreadable, and printed through _personal_path_safe at rc 2;\\n  - any other exception still hits the rc-2 catch-all;\\n  - no path returns 0 on failure.\\n- Nothing is written; reads use O_NOFOLLOW|O_NONBLOCK.\\n\\nNEW FINDINGS (annex)\\n\\nP1 — CHANGELOG.md:112-117 versus .claude/hooks/_lib/_contamination/cli_checks.py:131-138 and :193-261, and .claude/scripts/_contamination_inventory.py:28-144. Undeclared change to the verdict of a shipped CI gate, contradicted by the CHANGELOG.\\n- What the CHANGELOG says: CHANGELOG [1.4.4] says the split entry points \\\"keep their paths and their observable contracts\\\" and names check_contamination.py.\\n- What actually changed: the term rule (Rule 1) now fails closed. It returns rc 2 where v1.4.2/v1.4.3-rc.1 returned 0 in four cases:\\n  - (a) any tracked path ANYWHERE in the index is not valid UTF-8, or contains a literal U+FFFD (_index :46-52). Before, the path was decoded with errors=replace, read_bytes raised OSError, and the file was skipped. Rule 2 only refused such paths in docs/ or .claude/plans/.\\n  - (b) a tracked file exists but cannot be read, or is a FIFO, a device or a directory (_read_regular/_blob :58-95).\\n  - (c) a tracked symlink whose payload cannot be readlink'd (see P2-3).\\n  - (d) any disagreement between the walk and the index snapshots (:109-121).\\n- Other observable changes:\\n  - _SKIP_SUFFIXES no longer skips anything: regular .png/.pdf/.zip blobs that decode as UTF-8 are now matched.\\n  - The personal-path report now prints BEFORE the term report.\\n  - A Rule 2 rc 2 now returns before Rule 1 runs (cli_checks.py:208-212).\\n- None of this is in CHANGELOG [1.4.4], neither in a Fixed section nor in \\\"What an adopter should know\\\". Only the in-code census at check_contamination.py:439-469 states it.\\n- Failure scenario: an adopter's repository has one tracked file outside docs/ with a Latin-1 name, or a name that really contains U+FFFD. Their CI runs `bash .claude/scripts/check-contamination.sh` from templates/.github/workflows/validate.yml.template:87. It passes on v1.4.2. After `upgrade.sh --pin v1.4.4-rc.1` it exits 2 with \\\"a tracked Rule 1 path is not valid UTF-8\\\". Renaming is the only cure (no waiver exists), and the CHANGELOG told the adopter the contract had not changed.\\n- Impact: the direction is fail-closed, as §4 prescribes for a gate's input, and no session is blocked. The realistic trigger rate is low. The finding is the false CHANGELOG statement and the missing upgrade note.\\n- Minimal fix: add a CHANGELOG [1.4.4] Changed/Fixed bullet plus one line under \\\"What an adopter should know\\\", listing the new rc-2 classes (a)-(d), the end of the suffix skip, and the new report order. Alternatively, remove check_contamination.py from the \\\"same way / observable contracts\\\" sentence at :116.\\n\\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\\n\\nP2-1 — check_contamination.py:30-31 and _lib/_contamination/term_scan.py:21,31-45. The module docstring still says \\\"Binary file suffixes are excluded by extension\\\". find_violations takes skip_suffixes and never uses it, and scan_rule_one has no suffix test.\\n- test_check_contamination.py:145 test_binary_files_skipped still passes, but only because its \\\\x89 byte fails UTF-8 decoding, not because of the suffix.\\n- The fu144 test docstring (\\\"The suffix list is about file content\\\") implies the list was meant to stay for regular files.\\n- Fix: either restore the suffix skip for mode 100644/100755 blobs only, or delete the docstring sentence and the dead parameter, and rename or fix the test.\\n\\nP2-2 — _lib/_contamination/cli_checks.py:218-219. The comment says \\\"RULE 2 still runs below, as it does after a term hit\\\". Rule 2 now